WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.362
Julia was so terrified she could hardly breathe.

2
00:00:17.242 --> 00:00:18.743
Still, she didn't hesitate.

3
00:00:18.763 --> 00:00:23.186
"Stop!" she cried, leaping away from the time passage.

4
00:00:23.206 --> 00:00:25.908
"It's not Markos' fault.

5
00:00:26.468 --> 00:00:27.109
We'll stay."

6
00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:31.392
She glanced at Brody, but he appeared to be frozen in place.

7
00:00:32.468 --> 00:00:33.569
Julia couldn't believe it.

8
00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:40.074
Was he thinking about stepping through the passage despite Hermes' threats against Markos and his family?

9
00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:45.678
A second later she let out a sigh of relief as Brody stepped away from the passage too.

10
00:00:45.698 --> 00:00:49.860
"It's cool," he said.

11
00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:52.402
"I didn't really want to go anyway.

12
00:00:52.943 --> 00:00:55.284
I was totally looking forward to being in the Olympics."

13
00:00:55.304 --> 00:01:02.474
"You have a funny way of showing it, boy," Hermes snarled, though he sounded slightly less angry already.

14
00:01:02.494 --> 00:01:06.037
"Come. We need to have a talk about loyalty."

15
00:01:08.299 --> 00:01:12.162
As Hermes dragged Brody out of the room, Julia glanced at Markos.

16
00:01:13.283 --> 00:01:16.385
He'd taken a few steps forward and was staring through the passage.

17
00:01:17.506 --> 00:01:21.670
Julia glanced through at her own world just in time to see a car drive by.

18
00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:25.773
"Oh!" Markos exclaimed, pointing at it.

19
00:01:25.793 --> 00:01:27.494
"What was that?"

20
00:01:27.514 --> 00:01:30.445
"It's a car," Julia said.

21
00:01:30.465 --> 00:01:35.227
"It's like a wagon, except you don't need a horse or ox to pull it."

22
00:01:36.328 --> 00:01:37.549
Markos looked impressed.

23
00:01:37.569 --> 00:01:39.610
"Never mind.

24
00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:42.351
Let's step away from the time passage, shall we?"

25
00:01:42.712 --> 00:01:46.134
Caerus herded Markos and Julia into the outer room of the temple.

26
00:01:47.194 --> 00:01:49.235
The guard, now awake, was waiting there.

27
00:01:53.258 --> 00:01:58.504
so sorry, master," he said, cowering in front of Caerus.

28
00:01:58.544 --> 00:02:02.067
"I swear upon my life, I've never fallen asleep on the job before.

29
00:02:02.568 --> 00:02:03.669
It must have been some trick.

30
00:02:04.069 --> 00:02:08.633
Perhaps the mortals enlisted the aid of Hypnos or—" "Silence!"

31
00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:10.734
Caerus ordered, sounding annoyed.

32
00:02:10.754 --> 00:02:15.699
"I might forgive your incompetence just this once, mortal fool.

33
00:02:16.259 --> 00:02:21.363
But if you value your family and your sanity, you'll guard this chamber with your life from now

34
00:02:21.543 --> 00:02:23.585
on." "Of course.

35
00:02:23.845 --> 00:02:24.666
Thank you, Caerus!"

36
00:02:25.026 --> 00:02:26.688
The guard said quickly, bowing.

37
00:02:27.872 --> 00:02:29.634
"No mortal will get past me again!"

38
00:02:30.334 --> 00:02:32.516
As he turned away, he glared at the kids.

39
00:02:34.737 --> 00:02:35.978
Julia's heart sank.

40
00:02:37.119 --> 00:02:41.102
It was obvious that nobody was going to be able to sneak into the temple again before the

41
00:02:41.122 --> 00:02:45.445
Games. Besides, Hermes was aware of their plans now.

42
00:02:46.486 --> 00:02:50.549
If she and Brody escaped, Markos and his family would certainly suffer.

43
00:02:50.569 --> 00:02:54.792
"I guess we're stuck," she thought with a shiver.

44
00:02:56.152 --> 00:03:00.673
"We'll just have to hope that Hermes will keep his word and let us go after the Games."

45
00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:06.975
The next day Julia sat on the bench beside Markos.

46
00:03:08.055 --> 00:03:10.036
They were watching Brody's training session.

47
00:03:11.076 --> 00:03:14.457
He had already spent a couple of hours running and tossing the javelin.

48
00:03:15.697 --> 00:03:19.659
Now he was about to start practicing the long jump required for the pentathlon.

49
00:03:20.699 --> 00:03:24.560
That was a competition in which athletes competed in five different events.

50
00:03:26.004 --> 00:03:30.107
"Hermes is working Brody harder than ever today," Julia observed.

51
00:03:30.127 --> 00:03:34.270
"Does that mean he's still mad at us for trying to escape?"

52
00:03:35.551 --> 00:03:36.872
Markos looked thoughtful.

53
00:03:36.892 --> 00:03:39.393
"I doubt it," he said.

54
00:03:39.413 --> 00:03:42.896
"I mean, of course he was angry at the time.

55
00:03:43.536 --> 00:03:46.358
You're lucky he didn't turn us all into frogs or something."

56
00:03:47.319 --> 00:03:47.979
He shuddered.

57
00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:52.722
"However, I'm sure he's mostly forgotten about it by now."

58
00:03:54.284 --> 00:04:00.323
"Really?" Julia winced as Brody made his first attempt at the long jump and landed with a splat.

59
00:04:00.343 --> 00:04:03.985
"But Hermes kept saying how Brody betrayed him."

60
00:04:04.005 --> 00:04:07.187
"Yes," Markos said.

61
00:04:07.207 --> 00:04:11.389
"But remember, the gods view us as mortals view dogs.

62
00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:15.131
Would you really bother to hold a grudge against a dog?"

63
00:04:16.272 --> 00:04:17.193
Julia shrugged.

64
00:04:17.913 --> 00:04:22.816
She didn't like being compared to a dog, but she knew Markos didn't mean anything bad by it.

65
00:04:24.092 --> 00:04:27.033
"Thanks again for distracting Hera," she said.

66
00:04:27.053 --> 00:04:29.214
"That was really brave."

67
00:04:30.434 --> 00:04:31.674
Markos bowed his head.

68
00:04:31.694 --> 00:04:33.915
"You're welcome.

69
00:04:35.035 --> 00:04:36.756
Thanks for helping me in turn.

70
00:04:37.476 --> 00:04:40.317
You two could have easily escaped and left me to my fate."

71
00:04:41.718 --> 00:04:42.698
"We'd never do that.

72
00:04:43.118 --> 00:04:43.978
You're our friend."

73
00:04:44.398 --> 00:04:45.619
Julia smiled at him.

74
00:04:46.779 --> 00:04:49.320
Just then Hermes let out a shout of annoyance.

75
00:04:51.316 --> 00:04:55.117
Julia turned to look and saw that Brody had just attempted another jump.

76
00:04:56.278 --> 00:04:59.279
He was sprawled on the ground, panting and looking frustrated.

77
00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:03.280
"You're hopeless, boy!"

78
00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:04.620
Hermes cried.

79
00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:08.701
"How do you expect to win the pentathlon with that sort of performance?"

80
00:05:09.862 --> 00:05:14.243
Artemis and Apollo were watching from nearby, where their own athletes were boxing.

81
00:05:15.364 --> 00:05:16.344
Apollo snickered.

82
00:05:18.045 --> 00:05:22.768
"Do you really expect to beat Zeus' champion with that, Hermes?"

83
00:05:23.248 --> 00:05:23.809
he called.

84
00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:26.091
Hermes scowled at him.

85
00:05:26.111 --> 00:05:29.493
"Nobody asked your opinion, Apollo," he snapped.

86
00:05:30.654 --> 00:05:32.515
He spun around and pointed at Brody.

87
00:05:32.535 --> 00:05:36.858
"Again!" Brody groaned and climbed to his feet.

88
00:05:36.878 --> 00:05:41.061
"Okay," he said.

89
00:05:41.081 --> 00:05:44.584
"But we never had to do anything like this at football practice."

90
00:05:45.928 --> 00:05:47.269
Markos turned to Julia.

91
00:05:47.289 --> 00:05:49.310
"Do you think he'll improve?"

92
00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:50.971
He sounded worried.

93
00:05:50.991 --> 00:05:54.593
"Probably," Julia replied.

94
00:05:55.373 --> 00:05:57.755
"He's actually a very talented athlete.

95
00:05:58.375 --> 00:06:01.877
I mean, he picked up javelin throwing in about five minutes, remember?

96
00:06:02.277 --> 00:06:04.919
He beat Apollo's guy three times out of five."

97
00:06:06.099 --> 00:06:06.800
She grimaced.

98
00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:10.562
"That's not counting the time the javelins turned into snakes."

99
00:06:11.843 --> 00:06:12.803
Markos sighed.

100
00:06:14.984 --> 00:06:15.844
"I hope you're right."

101
00:06:16.404 --> 00:06:18.305
His gaze wandered around the field.

102
00:06:18.325 --> 00:06:22.106
"Because some of the other champions are looking pretty good.

103
00:06:22.566 --> 00:06:23.906
Not to mention Alcides.

104
00:06:24.747 --> 00:06:29.808
If that guy is even half as incredible as Zeus is claiming, none of the other athletes will

105
00:06:29.848 --> 00:06:30.608
have a chance."

106
00:06:31.889 --> 00:06:34.909
"Yeah." Julia didn't like to think about that.

107
00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:38.130
It was true that Brody was a good athlete.

108
00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:40.191
Maybe even a great one.

109
00:06:41.251 --> 00:06:44.312
Not that she'd ever tell him that—his ego was already big enough.

110
00:06:45.376 --> 00:06:48.577
But this was the Olympic Games, not a high school football game.

111
00:06:49.677 --> 00:06:50.878
And Brody was just a kid.

112
00:06:51.898 --> 00:06:54.198
What if he couldn't live up to Hermes' expectations?

113
00:06:55.279 --> 00:06:59.460
What if he couldn't beat a bunch of Greek champions who'd probably been training for this their whole

114
00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:03.881
lives? What would happen then to Brody—and to Julia?

115
00:07:04.961 --> 00:07:09.402
She cringed as Brody jumped again and Hermes let out a howl of dismay.

116
00:07:10.523 --> 00:07:14.744
She muttered to Markos, "I just hope Brody gets better fast."
